The legal texts are the Constitution of the Republic of Haiti of 29 March 1987 and its amendment published in Le Moniteur of 19 June 2012,
and the Code du travail as updated by the Decree of 24 February 1984 and the Loi du 5 juin 2003.

Official texts are not protected by copyright in Haiti. The Decree of 12 October 2005 on Copyright (Le Moniteur no. 23, 9 March 2006),
Article 5, says:

  "La protection prévue par le présent Décret ne s'étend pas : 1.- aux textes officiels de nature législative, administrative ou
  judiciaire, ni à leurs traductions officielles; ..."

Source of the bytes: Le Moniteur is not online, so the text is a copy by a third party, the Digithèque de matériaux juridiques et
politiques (MJP) of Jean-Pierre Maury, Université de Perpignan:
  https://mjp.univ-perp.fr/constit/ht1987.htm   (original 1987 text)
  https://mjp.univ-perp.fr/constit/ht2011.htm   (amended text; repealed words struck through, new words underlined)
Lexifina credits MJP as the host of these copies; the host's own commentary is not reproduced. The host's pages are unofficial.

The Code du travail is a copy by a third party, the Gender Equality Observatory of the United Nations Economic Commission for Latin
America and the Caribbean (CEPAL): https://oig.cepal.org/sites/default/files/2003_codtravail_hti.pdf. Lexifina credits CEPAL as the
host of this copy; it is unofficial.

